# OnyxOS — AI-Native Operating System for AR Glasses

An AI-first operating system that replaces traditional process scheduling with a **Lagrangian market-based agent economy**, purpose-built for wearable AI hardware (AR glasses) running on the **NVIDIA Jetson Orin Nano Super** (8GB, 67 TOPS, 1024 CUDA cores).

## YC Demo Strategy

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **The YC pitch is ~60 seconds.** The demo should showcase ONE jaw-dropping moment — not a feature tour.
>
> **The "Aha" moment:** Voice a command → OnyxOS's agents compete in real-time for GPU/RAM via a visible market auction → the winning agent runs inference → result is overlaid on a live camera feed — all on a $249 edge device.
>
> **Record a 10-15s video clip** rather than doing a live hardware demo on stage.

### What Makes This Innovative (YC Angle)
1. **No scheduler — a market.** Agents bid for compute using Lagrangian dual prices, not priority queues
2. **Physics-aware.** Thermal governor + power budget are first-class kernel primitives, not afterthoughts
3. **Graceful degradation.** Agents self-degrade (quantize models down) when resource prices spike — no OOM kills
4. **Edge-native.** Full LLM inference on a $249 device, no cloud required

